# Tools, tasks and hooks

Read this before changing `mise.toml`, `repos.toml`, the tasks in `mise-tasks/`, the scripts in `scripts/`, `hk.pkl`, sdd-kit, `ast-grep` rules and the tests in `tests/`.

## mise

mise installs all root tools and runs all tasks. The tools are listed in `[tools]` in `mise.toml`: Node 24, ast-grep, hk, pkl, rumdl, typos, agnix, and the OpenSpec CLI that `mise run kit:install` pins. Exact versions and checksums live in `mise.lock`, which the first `mise run setup` writes and which is committed. Update with `mise lock --bump`, then run `mise run test` and `mise run check`.

Node 24 runs the agent hook, the registry script, the sdd-kit checks and hooks.

## Repository registry

`repos.toml` is the only list of repositories. Each `[[repo]]` entry has `name`, `path` (always `repos/<name>`), `url`, `ref` (the rest branch), `branch_model` (`main-based` or `dev-based`, [branches.md](branches.md)) and `stack` (a free-text hint for agents).

Optional fields, written by `/bootstrap` or by hand, with paths relative to the clone:

| Field | Meaning | Shown in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `env_file`, `env_example` | The environment file the application reads and its example | the Environment row of the clone's command table in `AGENTS.md`, the table in `docs/agents/environment.md` |
| `env_notes` | What differs locally | the Notes column in `docs/agents/environment.md` |
| `test_needs` | What the clone's tests need, for example `PostgreSQL, the backend running` | under the clone's command table |
| `notes` | Anything else agents must know about the commands | under the clone's command table |
| `rules` | The clone's files agents read before editing it, a one-line list such as `["CLAUDE.md", ".claude/rules/"]` | above the clone's command table |

`scripts/repos.mjs` reads it, with no packages:

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `mise run add-repo` | Asks for repositories in a loop (URL, name, rest branch, branch model, stack), appends them to `repos.toml`, runs `sync` and offers to clone. `--yes` with `--name`, `--url`, `--ref`, `--branch-model` and `--stack` adds one repository without questions |
| `node scripts/repos.mjs set <name> key=value ...` | Sets optional fields of one entry (and `stack`), keeping every other line and comment, then runs `sync`. An empty value removes a field; `rules` takes comma-separated paths or an array such as `["CLAUDE.md", ".claude/rules/"]` |
| `mise run repos:sync` | Regenerates everything that lists the repositories, between marker comments |
| `mise run repos:check` | Fails when `repos.toml` and the generated files disagree; part of `mise run check` |

`sync` writes:

| File | Section |
| --- | --- |
| `mise.toml` | `[bootstrap.repos]` between `# repos:begin` and `# repos:end`, kept last in the file |
| `openspec/clones` | the sdd-kit clone list between `# repos:begin` and `# repos:end`, only when `openspec/` exists |
| `AGENTS.md` | the command tables (`<!-- repos:begin:commands -->`), with each clone's extra tasks from `mise-tasks/<name>/`, and the branch rules (`<!-- repos:begin:branches -->`) |
| `docs/agents/branches.md` | the table of clones and their branch models (`<!-- repos:begin -->`) |
| `repos/README.md` | the clone table (`<!-- repos:begin -->`) |
| `docs/agents/environment.md` | the environment file table (`<!-- repos:begin:env -->`), only when the markers exist |
| `mise-tasks/<name>/` | the stubs `test`, `check`, `run` and `install`, only when missing |

Text outside the markers is never touched, and the generated text follows the project language (`language` in `.copier-answers.yml`). Do not edit inside the markers by hand: the next `sync` overwrites it and `check` reports it.

A stub task changes into the clone and fails with "command not configured yet". `/bootstrap` in Claude Code, or a developer, replaces its last line with the clone's own command and deletes the `# repos:stub` comment; `sync` never overwrites an existing task file. `mise run setup` skips an `install` task that is still a stub.

To remove a repository, delete its entry from `repos.toml`, run `mise run repos:sync` and delete `mise-tasks/<name>/`; `check` reports a leftover task folder.

## Tasks

Each task is a separate executable file in `mise-tasks/`, listed in [../../mise-tasks/README.md](../../mise-tasks/README.md). The `<name>:*` tasks repeat nothing from the clones. They change into the clone folder, call its own command and return its exit code. If the clone is missing, the task fails with a message naming the clone and `mise run clone`.

`mise run pull` updates the meta-repository first and then every clone, each on its current branch, with `git pull --rebase --autostash`. A failed pull, a conflict, a leftover stash or a missing clone is listed under "Not updated, resolve manually" and fails the task; a conflicting rebase is left in progress. A repository on a branch without upstream is listed under "No upstream, not updated" and does not fail the task.

## sdd-kit

The template ships no sdd-kit files and no OpenSpec version. `mise run kit:install` (run by the first `mise run setup`) and `mise run kit:update` call `scripts/kit.sh`:

1. Picks the version: `SDD_KIT_REF` when set; for `install` the version already installed; otherwise the highest release tag of `https://github.com/cmdtorch/sdd_kit.git` (`git ls-remote --tags`, pre-releases left out).
2. Reads the OpenSpec version the kit needs from `npx github:cmdtorch/sdd_kit#<tag> --version` and pins it with `mise use "npm:@fission-ai/openspec@<version>"`.
3. Runs the kit's installer with `--yes`, `--metarepo` with the clones from `repos.toml` and `--questions-language` from the project language. The installer writes `openspec/`, the kit skills, commands and agents in `.claude/`, merges its hooks and permissions into `.claude/settings.json` and adds its lines to `.gitignore`.
4. Runs `mise run repos:sync` so `openspec/clones` carries the generated markers, then the kit's health check `node openspec/tooling/bin/doctor.mjs`.

Everything the kit writes is committed: `openspec/`, `.claude/`, `.gitignore` and `mise.toml`, and `mise.lock` and `.mise/locks/` (the OpenSpec CLI's dependency lock) when present. The whole team then works with one kit version without installing it, and an update arrives as a reviewable pull request. Kit files are never edited by hand; the installer keeps a hash manifest and does not overwrite a locally edited file.

## Single check

`mise run check` runs independent steps and prints a result table. Each step runs even if the previous one failed.

| Step | What it runs |
| --- | --- |
| `<name>` | `mise run <name>:check` in each clone: its own linters and type checks |
| `code-rules` | `ast-grep test` and `ast-grep scan` over the clones; without rules the step reports `no rules` |
| `repos` | `scripts/repos.mjs check`: `repos.toml` against `mise.toml`, `openspec/clones`, the task folders and the generated docs |

Clone tests are not included; they usually need a database or a running stack. If a clone's own check already fails on its rest branch, the reason goes into [../clone-backlog.md](../clone-backlog.md), and `check` stays red until it is fixed in the clone.

## Root lint

`mise run lint` checks only the meta-repository's files.

- `rumdl` checks Markdown, configured in `.rumdl.toml`.
- `typos` checks spelling, configured in `_typos.toml`.
- `agnix --strict` checks agent settings, configured in `.agnix.toml`.
- `scripts/check-agent-files.sh` fails on `CLAUDE.md`, `CLAUDE.local.md` and `.claude/CLAUDE.md` in the root, and on a relative link in `AGENTS.md` that points to a missing file.

The clones in `repos/` and the changes and specs in `openspec/` are not checked. Neither are the files that OpenSpec and sdd-kit install and overwrite on update: the `openspec-*` skills, commands in `.claude/commands/`, agents in `.claude/agents/`, `openspec/protocols/`, `openspec/schemas/` and `openspec/tooling/`.

## Meta-repository git hooks

`mise run setup` installs the hooks with `hk install --mise`. They run only in the meta-repository's git and are not installed into the clones. The clones have their own hooks, installed by the clones' own install commands.

- `pre-commit` checks, for the committed files, the syntax of the tasks in `mise-tasks/`, `mise tasks validate`, the format of `mise.toml`, and the rule tests when `ast-grep/` changes.
- `pre-push` runs `mise run lint`.

## Meta-repository tests

`mise run test` runs each `tests/*.sh` in its own temporary folder. The tests create throwaway git repositories as stand-in clones and a copy of the meta-repository, and check the tasks, the registry script and the agent hook against them. They need neither the real clones, nor sdd-kit, nor the network. Shared helpers live in `tests/lib.sh`.

## Template updates

The project was generated from the sdd-metarepo Copier template; the answers are in `.copier-answers.yml`. `uvx copier update --trust` brings the template's improvements as a diff to review. Files the template generated and the project changed get conflict markers; the generated sections and `repos.toml` belong to the project and are refreshed with `mise run repos:sync` after the update.
